   122	## 4. Correctness contracts
   123	
   124	These hold on every composition. Where a contract's safety rests on unproven engine behavior, a falsifier must pass first, and
   125	a failed falsifier blocks dependent work.
   126	
   127	- **C1 read-layer eligibility.** A derived read layer serves a read only when, for the whole query: the scope matches the
   128	  engine's ownership record; its mapping generation equals the release the reader requires; recorded time is absent (explicit
   129	  recorded time takes the exact path, because recorded timestamps are not monotonic in commit order); the position is one the
   130	  layer holds exactly (latest publication, or for XTDB a physical commit boundary); the valid instant is one it holds exactly
   131	  (QLever: inside the publication's window and not maintaining); and no partial, stale or conflicted entity touches a referenced
   132	  attribute. Otherwise the whole query takes the exact path in the same native language.
   133	- **C2 QLever commit protocol (when QLever is the source of truth).** The host broker fsyncs one framed, pure-quad-delta log frame
   134	  per commit group (`F_FULLFSYNC`): that is the irrevocable decision. Group members are validated against a staged prefix. One
   135	  guarded update operation applies the group (marker `(epoch, position)` in the WHERE clause, change counts checked). QLever's
   136	  snapshot swap is publication; the ACK follows publication; verification is post-publication; uncertainty fences the lane;
   137	  re-send is the first repair; a retry returns success only after publication (`CommitPending` or `Repairing` before that).
   138	  Checkpoints are folded from the log; rebuilds use crash-safe generation selection.
   139	- **C3 one mutator per QLever store.** The broker (or, for a read layer, the feed maintainer) holds a host kernel lock, writes an
   140	  `EPOCH_BEGIN` frame, guards every update with the marker, and treats the access token as visible.
   141	- **C4 publication and maintenance (QLever).** The marker records `(P, validInstant, nextBoundary, state)`; boundary maintenance runs
   142	  in bounded chunks computed at apply time; repository and qualified raw reads refuse or take the exact path while `MAINTAINING`.
   143	- **C5 conflicts.** Equal duplicates are one value with several supports; a conflict is a card-one attribute with two or more
   144	  distinct live values; repository reads fail with `ConflictingValuesError`; the raw convenience shape is documented as not
   145	  equivalent; the canonical conflict-aware relation is `values(attribute)`.
   146	- **C6 journal.** The logical journal stays queryable as documented; physical slimming only with synthesized, byte-identical facts.
   147	- **C7 scope and tenant isolation.** One scope per engine in production with an enforced ownership record; shared engines use
   148	  scope-qualified storage and collision tests. Tenant isolation at the storage layer is a requirement.
   149	- **C8 reads never mutate.** Every read API, including recursion, the Datalog `rules` path and maintained queries, is read-only;
   150	  recursion uses the shared frontier loop with budgets, then engine-native fast paths that must match it (R10).
