   204	### 6.4 Gates, receipts and evidence
   205	
   206	| Gate | What it runs | Needs engine |
   207	| --- | --- | --- |
   208	| G0 | typecheck and pure unit tests | no |
   209	| G1 | unchanged44 shared conformance, current and reopen | yes |
   210	| G2 | native142 (71 tasks); XTQL and SQL counted separately, every substep | yes |
   211	| G3 | entity suite: repository and raw queries against the independent oracle, plus mutation controls | yes |
   212	| G4 | semantic counterexamples with original expected answers | yes |
   213	| G5 | write semantics: duplicates, CAS conflicts, unknown outcomes, crash and reopen, C2 crash matrix | yes |
   214	| NS | north-star benchmark: P1 to P5 on the fixed writer trace (`lab/TARGETS.md` sections 1 and 2) | yes, scale window for large rungs |
   215	| GS | the 20 golden scenarios (`lab/TARGETS.md` section 6) | yes, scale window |
   216	
   217	Receipts bind what executed (source including uncommitted and untracked inputs, lockfile, toolchain, imported `dist` hashes, gate
   218	and oracle hashes, spec and log versions, fixture contents, raw-result hashes, endpoint, engine image and configuration, counts,
   219	first failures, timings, co-runners, resource peaks). Gates fail closed on skips, zero cases, missing identities or wrong endpoints.
   220	Bytes of executed inputs and raw outcomes are retained under `runs/objects/`. Gate and oracle changes need verifier review, and
   221	Codex review when they change what an obligation accepts. Whether an obligation is closed is decided by `lab/acceptance/`.
