    42	### 0.1.0-draft
    43	
    44	First draft (88 obligations). Superseded.
    45	
    46	## 1. How to read this contract
    47	
    48	- **One obligation is one binary fact.** It has an id, a statement, lanes, case selections, oracles, entrypoints, profiles, a closure (rules, modes, thresholds), mutation controls, the PLAN contracts it traces, sources, a grounding label and a verifier mode.
    49	- **Every status is OPEN.** No acceptance receipt exists for any obligation.
    50	- **Authority for goals and targets.** `lab/SCOPE.md`, `lab/NORTH-STAR.md`, `lab/TARGETS.md` and `lab/research/SAM-pasted-numbers-2026-11-07.md` (Sam, 2026-11-07), compiled with `RULINGS.md` into `obligations.json`. Correctness is the floor on every priority: a fast wrong answer scores zero.
    51	- **Values this contract chose.** Thresholds whose source says `derived`, the reader read mix and window lengths in `load-contract.json`, and the A0 allowances in `budgets.json` are values no source states; they are fixed so evaluation is mechanical, and changing one is a contract version.
    52	- **Artifacts.** `obligations.json` (authority), `load-contract.json`, `budgets.json`, `capability-matrix.md`, this file. All generated.
    53	
    54	## 2. Done predicate (PLAN v1.1 section 1)
    55	
    56	```
    57	done(T) = for one identified integrated profile T per surface
    58	          AND over lanes { xtdb-xtql, xtdb-sql, qlever-sparql }
    59	          AND over sections { G1..G10, R, S, L }
    60	            closed(section, lane, T)
    61	          with every receipt FRESH on T (no carry-forward into final acceptance)
    62	
    63	 retained evidence --> VC / VA / VM / VV validity --> closure rules recompute verdicts --> obligation
    64	   (runs/objects)       (acyclic: VC <- VA <- VM, VV)    from retained bytes             --> section --> lane --> done
    65	```
    66	
    67	
    68	Status algorithm:
    69	
    70	```
    71	for each lane L and integrated profile T:
    72	  for each obligation O with L in O.lanes:
    73	    key = L if O.receiptScope == 'lane' else engineOfLane[L]
    74	    A = acceptance receipts for (O.id, key) on T that pass VA (using VC records they cite)
    75	    closed(O, L, T) = O.grounding != 'policy-pending' and every case set of O is pinned
    76	                      and A non-empty and every rule in O.closure.rules holds by its recompute
    77	                      and VV-valid verifier coverage exists per VERIFIER_MODES[verifierMode(O)]
    78	  closed(section, L, T) = all closed(O, L, T) for O with section in O.goals
    79	done(T) = closed for every section and lane, with every receipt fresh on T (APPLICABILITY.finalAcceptance)
    80	```
    81	
    82	**Lane accounting.** Every read substep records exactly one language: xtql (native.select), sql (selectSql), sparql (QLever native). A lane receipt counts a task only when every relational substep is in the lane's language. A task with a relational substep in another language, or with a host step not listed below, counts for neither XTDB language.
    83	
    84	| Permitted host step | Source | Rule |
    85	| --- | --- | --- |
    86	| HS-NORMALIZE | RULINGS Q3 | A declared normalization step that reads no data: arithmetic or classification over values already returned by native substeps of the same task (for example BigInt subtraction of two returned sums). It is declared in the frozen task recipe, recorded in the trace, and its time is counted inside the task's measured call. |
    87	| HS-FRONTIER | PLAN C8 | C8 frontier control for recursive reads, limited to the operations in FRONTIER_RULES. All relational evaluation stays native at one fixed cut. |
    88	
    89	**C8 frontier control (HS-FRONTIER).**
    90	
    91	- Permitted host operations: deduplicate returned frontier ids; subtract the visited set from the new frontier; test termination (empty frontier, maxRounds reached, maxRecursiveRows reached); bind the next frontier as query parameters, chunked so each native query stays within its declared parameter bound; count rows and rounds against the bounds.
    92	- Forbidden host operations: filtering on values, types, entity types or time; joins between returned relations; visibility, cut or valid-time evaluation; negation, aggregation, ordering or pagination of answers; any read that does not go through the lane's native language.
    93	- fixedCut: Every round runs at the same captured basis (scope, P, optional R, V); each round's trace records that basis and the evaluator checks they are identical.
    94	- bounds: maxRounds and maxRecursiveRows are declared per task. Reaching a bound fails with the typed recursion-limit error (ERROR_TABLE E-RECURSION-LIMIT) and returns no partial answer.
    95	- cost: Host frontier time and peak host memory are counted inside the task's measured cost and reported per round.
    96	- noMutation: No round writes engine state (engine-side mutation count unchanged across the read).
    97	- accounting: A task whose host steps are only HS-FRONTIER (and HS-NORMALIZE) operations counts as pure in the lane's language.
