   177	### 4.3 Comparisons and group identity
   178	
   179	| Id | Rule | Source |
   180	| --- | --- | --- |
   181	| CMP-SAME | same family: exact comparison (integer as integers, binary64 by IEEE value, text by Unicode codepoint sequence, datetime by instant, boolean false < true, ref by id codepoints) | exact typing |
   182	| CMP-NUMERIC-CONST | an untyped numeric constant compares by numeric value with number and datetime values (number 7 and datetime 7 both equal 7); text '7' is not equal | testkit 'datalog equality predicates compare numeric values as numbers' (packages/testkit/src/index.ts:721) |
   183	| CMP-INT-FLOAT | integer versus number: equality is false and they never share a group; an ordered comparison across them is preflight E-MIXED-FAMILY unless converted explicitly | RULINGS Q8d (core silent for stored integer versus number) |
   184	| CMP-IDENTITY | entity ids and ref identities compare only with text or ref constants; a numeric or boolean constant is never equal and != is true | testkit 'datalog equality keeps identity bindings string-typed' |
   185	| CMP-UNTYPED-STRING | an untyped string constant matches string and ref values; a typed ref constant matches only ref values | testkit 'datalog untyped strings match string and ref values while typed refs stay exact' |
   186	| CMP-BOOL-INT | boolean true and integer 1 are distinct values and distinct groups | packet oracle identity() (event_oracles.py: bool true vs i64 one) |
   187	| CMP-NEGZERO | -0.0 and +0.0 are one value for identity, grouping and set membership; when supports differ only in representation, the returned representation is the one from the support with the lowest recorded position; a single-assertion read returns the stored representation | RULINGS Q14b; packages/core/src/content/CanonicalJson.ts:77 |
