   211	| CN-NEW-OR-WORSENED | with enforcement on, a command is rejected only when its post-state creates a new violation or worsens an existing one at some represented valid-time boundary; a pre-existing violation does not block an unrelated command and stays readable | packages/core/src/Constraint.ts:376 (newlyViolated) |
   212	| CN-CARD-COUNT | write-time cardinality counts live assertions, including equal-valued duplicates (unchanged) | Constraint.ts:193; PLAN C5.1 |
   213	| CN-PREEXISTING-CONFLICT | a card-one conflict that predates the enforcing write stays a conflict (C5.2) and reads per C5.3 | PLAN C5.2 |
