     8	| Q1 unrestricted raw exactness | Not required for done. Required instead: (a) the repository and every supported native fragment are exact over the full Triplex value domain; (b) the raw dataset is exact on its documented exact channels (order keys, lexical channels, native typed literals inside their exact ranges); (c) raw natively typed shapes outside exact ranges (raw `ORDER BY STR` on QLever, raw correlated NOT EXISTS with filter-only correlation, raw int64 beyond ±2^59 on QLever, raw `SUM` over BIGINT on XTDB) are KNOWN-LIMIT rows with retained counterexamples and a raw-query guide entry. Engine repairs are pursued only when a required surface needs them. Exceptions are per cell (engine, language, surface, operator, value domain), never per row (Codex acceptance review #2): QLever's bounded numerics do not exempt XTDB arithmetic. Every exempted raw cell names its exact mapped recipe (for example XTDB `SUM(CAST(x AS DECIMAL(38,0)))` instead of raw `SUM` over BIGINT, QLever order-key ordering instead of `ORDER BY STR`) and the obligation that qualifies that recipe; the original raw failure stays as a diagnostic with its unchanged expected answer. Supported fragments have a fixed minimum coverage set listed in the contract, so an operation cannot be removed from the advertised surface to avoid a failure. | handoff README: "Raw SPARQL numeric behavior is narrower than the full Triplex value domain; use the declared mapping and retain unsupported cases"; START-HERE 4: an encoded key "does not make arbitrary SPARQL STR compliant" |
     9	| Q2 load bar | A fixed minimum is part of done, because "efficient" must mean something beyond the rate16 floor. At 256 logical clients on the 10m-entity representative dataset, open-loop offered load of 1 request per client per second (256 requests/s; 90% reads by the query mix, 10% writes, so 25.6 commands/s): correctness-qualified read goodput ≥ 0.99 of offered reads; explicit rejections ≤ 0.01; per-client fairness ≥ 0.9; read latency p99 ≤ 1 s for point/entity/repository classes and ≤ 5 s for analytic classes; write visibility p99 ≤ 2 s; every writer visible inside 30 s. Stress at 512 and 1024: zero correctness violations, explicit rejections counted, goodput retention ≥ 0.9 of the 256-level goodput, recovery to the 256-level bar within 60 s after stress. The four previously unsourced floors (goodput 0.99, rejections 0.01, fairness 0.9, retention 0.9) are adopted by this ruling. Calibration still runs first; if calibration shows a number is physically impossible on this VM for every candidate, the orchestrator records the measurement and asks Sam before lowering it. | goal ambition ("efficient", 256 logical clients with steady writes); review r1 #2 (explicit experimental criteria, no invented production SLA) |
