    62	| Q16 derived thresholds | History flatness 1.1 (current-pull p99 and bytes read at history depth 10 ≤ 1.1x depth 1) stands. Reader basis mix is 80% at the latest committed tx (named exactly, the reconcile pull), 15% at a tx within the last hour (in-flight reconciles and sweeps pinned to an older position), 5% at a past basis up to 90 days back (explain and audit); the draft's 25% at 30 days overweighted cold reads, which the paste marks COLD. Warmup 120 s and 600 s per ladder level stand for acceptance runs; a shorter screening profile (30 s warmup, 120 s per level) is allowed for candidate comparison and can never close an obligation. Budget allowances (write bytes 4.0x, ingest 0.5x, memory 1.5x, disk 2.0x of the A0 control at the same rung) stand as provisional and are re-frozen after EXP-N02 measures the controls, before any candidate is compared. | Sam's paste: reconcile pull HOT at the current basis, explain/audit COLD; TARGETS section 1 |
    63	| Q17 sparse profile | Dropping the separate sparse profile is accepted; scenario GS.15 (one large tenant and 1,000 small ones) covers population skew. | rescoped targets |
    64	| Q18 decimal kind | A decimal attribute declares precision and scale. Values are stored as scaled integers (when precision ≤ 15 so the scaled value stays within 2^53) or as order-preserving decimal strings; a value with more fractional digits than the scale, or outside the precision, is rejected with a typed error, never rounded. Decimal is its own family, ordered between number and datetime in the card-many family order; comparison between decimal and integer or number is a typed preflight error unless the query converts explicitly; arithmetic runs in the TypeScript kernel with exact decimal arithmetic. | Sam's corrected numeric rule |
    65	| Q19 engine-side exact sums | Needed only where a projection sums many rows. EXP-X02 confirms the XTDB recipe (R14 measured `SUM(CAST(x AS DECIMAL(32,0)))` exact and free on 2.2.0; the split-sum is the fallback); EXP-F02 cross-checks. | corrected numeric rule item 5 |
    66	| Q20 Q8a/Q8b wording | Q8a and Q8b now read "integer" rather than "int64": exact totals with a typed error only when the final result is outside the engine's exact range, and engine-side sums only where a projection needs them; per-subject sums run in the kernel (BigInt). AVG over integers keeps Q8b's preflight rule. | corrected numeric rule |

