380:### 5.6 Closure rules
384:| CR-PASS-ALL | case-result | VA | each case verdict = comparator(oracle expected, retained raw result bytes) | every resolved case passes in every declared mode |
385:| CR-COUNTEREXAMPLE | case-result | VA | as CR-PASS-ALL, with the original oracle file whose hash is unchanged since the first recorded failure | every original counterexample passes with unedited case text |
386:| CR-MUTANT-KILL | mutation-record, case-result | VM, VA | reach hits from the retained probe log; killing assertions re-compared from retained expected and observed objects | every listed mutant meets MUTANT_RULE and the clean receipt passes |
387:| CR-OBSERVE | observation | VA | O-OBS verdict per protocol from retained samples and events | every required protocol verdict is PASS within the obligation's thresholds |
388:| CR-FAULT | fault-witness, case-result | VA | expected outcome chosen from the last witnessed transition in COMMIT_OUTCOMES (or the case's declared outcome), compared with final state, caller outcome, retries and post-recovery case results | every fault point injected at least T-FAULT-REPS times and every injection matches |
389:| CR-STATIC | static-witness | VA | CMP-DIAGNOSTICS on retained tsc output; any-scan re-run | observed diagnostics equal expected exactly and the any-scan is empty |
390:| CR-SCALE | scale-dataset, case-result, observation | VA | population counts versus O-REPLAY analytic counts; sample verdicts by comparator; capacity verdict by OBS-RESOURCE | counts equal, every sample passes, run admitted and within envelope |
391:| CR-PERF | case-result, observation, plan-record | VA, VC | latency and ratio statistics from retained timings | every named threshold met in each of 3 independent runs |
392:| CR-METRICS | observation | VA | metric values from retained samples | every listed metric present and measured |
393:| CR-NS | ns-run | VA, VC | every named NS bar from retained raw events: goodput counts only reads whose answer equals O-REPLAY at the read's named basis; latencies from offer; ratios against the same run's baselines; per-core throughput from the recorded engine core count | every named bar met in each of T-RUNS independent runs, on the fixed writer trace of load-contract.json |
394:| CR-GS | ns-run, case-result, fault-witness | VA, VC | scenario correctness verdicts from retained answers against O-REPLAY or O-HAND, commit and feed integrity from retained receipts and feed entries, and every named bar from retained raw events | zero wrong answers, zero lost or duplicated commits, zero feed gaps or order violations, every named bar met, in each of T-RUNS runs, on every compared composition |
395:| CR-REQUIREMENT | requirement-route, case-result | VA | each test verdict from retained results; the route record checked for a plain statement when WORKAROUND | the engine declares NATIVE or a documented WORKAROUND and every test of the requirement passes on that route; an OPEN requirement never excludes the engine from comparison |
396:| CR-CALIBRATION | calibration-record | VC | VC3 check of each value against the registry | a VC-valid record exists for every L-* threshold of the lane |
397:| CR-MATRIX | case-result | VA | matrix cells from obligations.json capabilityMatrix and the cited receipts | every required cell EXACT with a receipt; every raw-required KNOWN-LIMIT cell has its exception record and guide entry |
398:| CR-PROVENANCE | provenance-manifest | VA | manifest inputs compared with the guide and docs hashes | inputs are only the raw-query guide and engine public docs; the author is a fresh agent |
399:| CR-WITNESS | observation, case-result | VA | OBS-WORK work-unit ratios from retained engine-side counters | every named witness threshold met and answers equal the no-reuse or fresh-recompute run |
400:| CR-BUDGET | budget-record, observation | VA | complete-path cost and NS measurements from retained evidence against budgets.json | within the absolute bars and caps and within the A0-relative allowances at every rung, compared cumulatively against the frozen A0 control |
