   506	### 6.1 O-REPLAY (independent Python event replay)
   507	
   508	- **Inputs.** The captured command intent (ordered submissions with operations, typed values in canonical encoding, entity ids and types, valid intervals, preconditions, meta, enforcement mode and rules, nested-transaction structure), schema releases, and durable-decision evidence (engine commit evidence or the log of record read back, and the fault witness). ACK receipts bind only generated identities: assertion ids, txIds and recorded instants.
   509	- **Clocks.** Recorded instants are not assumed monotonic in position order; separate runtimes supply their own clocks (PLAN C1). Histories with equal and with decreasing recorded instants are first-class cases (EV-SAME-R, EV-DECREASING-R, CS-TEMPORAL decreasing-clock).
   510	- **R independent of P.** A cut is (scope, P, optional R, V). Recorded visibility is `recordedPosition <= P` and, when R is bound, `recordedAt <= R`, evaluated independently: an assertion with a later position but an earlier instant is invisible at P below its position, and an assertion at a lower position with an instant above R is invisible at R.
   511	- **Position accounting.** Positions are derived by the oracle from the committed order: one position per Triplex transact, nested transacts inside one outer transaction take consecutive positions in callback order and share one engine commit; the oracle checks every receipt position against its own and fails the run on a mismatch.
   512	- **Outcomes.** The oracle derives each command's expected outcome from intent, order, preconditions, enforcement (CN-NEW-OR-WORSENED) and durable-decision evidence (COMMIT_OUTCOMES), then compares the receipts' outcomes afterwards. A receipt never decides which command is valid or committed.
   513	- **Outputs.** Complete assertion metadata; raw-lifetime and as-of snapshot history; entity models (card-one value or E-CONFLICTING-VALUES per C5; card-many per CARD_MANY_ORDER; absent optional as a missing property; includes at the same basis; timelines); transaction records with ordered changes and the logical journal facts (C6); cursor page sequences; support counts; C1 eligibility routes (for O-PLAN); arithmetic, comparison and aggregate results per section 4; analytic scale counts per population stratum (SCALE_POPULATION, section S).
   514	- **Independence.** Python stdlib only; imports no repository code; its own exact integers and decimals, IEEE binary64 (via struct) and codepoint ordering; no casefolding.
   515	- **Self-checks before ACCEPTED.** Reproduce O-HAM finite-nine, O-CFG8 tiny-v4 and the O-EVT cut semantics where domains overlap; unit tests for every table row of section 4.
   516	
   517	### 6.2 O-SHAPE
   518	
   519	Each case file entry carries: resultSemantics: set | bag | ordered; groupingKey: list of variables with COMPARISON_RULES identity; unboundHandling: exclude-row | null-cell (stated per projected variable); comparator: CMP-SET-ROWS | CMP-BAG-ROWS | CMP-ORDERED-ROWS; expectedRows; citation (SPARQL 1.1 or SQL section, or the packet task).
   520	
   521	- Packet-derived shapes use set semantics (runner sorted-unique comparison).
   522	- Negation controls compare the projected entity set.
   523	- Aggregate controls follow AGGREGATE_RULES; empty groups per AG-EMPTY-*.
   524	- Tied extremes keep every witness row (AG-MINMAX-TIES).
   525	- An unbound projected variable is a null cell only where the case says null-cell; otherwise the row is excluded.
