   296	### 5.3 Selector semantics
   297	
   298	An obligation's cases are a list of {set, select}. select is a list of tags or named required case ids; 'all' selects every case of the set. The evaluator resolves the selection against the set's pinned manifest (lab/acceptance/cases/<set>.json, sha256 pinned in the contract version): the selected cases are those carrying any listed tag, plus any named case listed by id. The resolution must be non-empty, every listed entry must be in the set's requiredTags or requiredCases, and every requiredCases id must exist in the manifest. A set whose manifest is not pinned in the contract version cannot close any obligation. Declared executions = selected cases x modes (x 1 per receipt scope key).
   299	
   300	### 5.4 Threshold registry
   301	
   302	Calibration may only tighten a threshold (a smaller max, a larger min) or record it UNATTAINABLE with the measurement. Loosening any value needs Sam (TARGETS threshold policy); until he rules, the obligation stays OPEN.
