   527	### 6.3 O-OBS protocols
   528	
   529	| Protocol | Evidence fields | Verdict |
   530	| --- | --- | --- |
   531	| OBS-CANCEL | requestId, connectionId, tCancelRequested, tCallerSettled, callerError, transportAck {kind, t}, engineActiveSamples [{t, activeQueryIds}], tDrained, reuseQueryId, tReuseOk | PASS iff callerError matches E-CANCELLED or E-TIMEOUT as the case pins, transportAck observed, the request id absent from every engine sample after tDrained with tDrained - tCancelRequested <= T-DRAIN-MS, sample gaps <= 1000 ms over [tCancelRequested, tDrained + 5000 ms], and the reuse query on the same connection succeeds |
   532	| OBS-PREABORT | requestId, engineStatementLog [{t, tag}], coverage | PASS iff zero engine statements carry the request id over the full coverage window |
   533	| OBS-CONNECTIONS | poolDeclarations [{label, max}], engineConnectionSamples [{t, label, count}], baseline, tClose | PASS iff every sample <= declared max and the count equals baseline within T-CONN-RELEASE-MS after tClose |
   534	| OBS-SCRATCH | relation, countBefore, countAfter, resolutionReceipts | PASS iff countAfter = countBefore for every scratch relation and every unknown working outcome is resolved |
   535	| OBS-NO-MUTATION | engineMutationCounterBefore, engineMutationCounterAfter, counterSource | PASS iff the engine's committed-transaction or update counter is unchanged across the read |
   536	| OBS-RESOURCE | forecast {memory, disk}, peaks [{owner, rss, disk, t}], envelope | PASS iff every peak <= forecast <= envelope (and <= T-PLANNER-MEM-BYTES where named) |
   537	| OBS-AVAILABILITY | tFailure, probes [{t, kind: write\|read, outcome}] | PASS iff a write and a read both succeed at some t <= tFailure + T-AVAIL-WINDOW-MS with no manual restart event |
   538	| OBS-SCALE-COUNT | population, countQueryCaseResult, analyticCount | PASS iff the count query's answer equals O-REPLAY's analytic count |
   539	| OBS-WORK | operation, engineWorkUnits {rowsScanned, rowsWritten, triplesTouched, bytesWritten}, source | ratio of work units between the compared operations, evaluated against the named witness threshold |
   540	| OBS-MAINTENANCE | kind, tStart, tEnd, lagSamples | events present; lag statistics against the named threshold |
   541	| OBS-FAULT-TRANSITIONS | transition, t, durableEvidenceObject | the last witnessed transition is the last one whose durable evidence is present after the crash |
   542	
   543	### 6.4 O-PLAN protocols
   544	
   545	| Protocol | Evidence fields | Verdict |
   546	| --- | --- | --- |
   547	| OBS-PLAN-ROUTE | queryId, route: projection \| exact, eligibilityInputs {scopeOwner, mappingGeneration, recordedTimeBound, positionKind, validInstant, markerState, partialOrConflictedReferenced} | PASS iff route equals O-REPLAY's C1 model: projection only when every C1 condition holds for the whole query |
   548	| OBS-PLAN-ACCESS | queryId, enginePlanObject, accessPathClass | key-bounded iff the XTDB plan uses an _id IID selector (scan.clj selector) for the probed table, or the QLever plan's first operation is an index scan with the subject or predicate-object bound; otherwise scan |
   549	| OBS-PLAN-COST | queryId, declaredBudget, estimate, actual | PASS iff actual <= declaredBudget, or the query stopped with the pinned error at the budget |
   550	
   551	### 6.5 O-SPEC rules
   552	
   553	- Positive witnesses assert exact types with an Equals<A, B> helper; assignability alone does not count.
   554	- Every asserted type is also checked not to be any (IsAny<T> is false); an accidental any fails.
   555	- Negative witnesses do not use @ts-expect-error; tsc runs on the witness set and the observed set of {file, line, column, code} must equal the pinned expected set exactly (CMP-DIAGNOSTICS); an unrelated diagnostic fails.
   556	- The emitted public declarations are scanned: no exported symbol resolves to any except an explicitly listed allowlist in the witness manifest.
   557	- Witnesses import only from packed public package exports, compiled with the consumer's strict tsconfig.
