   616	### 7.1 Value types (CS-TYPES8, CS-TYPES8-NEG, CS-WIDEN)
   617	
   618	| Family | Edge values |
   619	| --- | --- |
   620	| string | "", ASCII mixed case A E c z, NFC U+00E9 and NFD e U+0301 as distinct values, U+E000, U+10000, U+1F600, quote, backslash, CR, LF, a 64 KiB text |
   621	| integer | 0, 1, -1, 2^53-1, -(2^53-1) on every lane; 2^53+1, 2^59-1, -2^59 where the lane accepts them; values beyond the lane's range belong to CS-RANGE-OUT |
   622	| decimal | 0.00, 16.50, 16.49, 1e11 cents as a scaled integer, a negative value, an order-preserving string encoding round trip (CS-DECIMAL covers scale overflow) |
   623	| number (binary64, approximate values only) | +0.0, -0.0, 0.1, 0.30000000000000004, 1.0000000000000002, 2^53 as a double, 5e-324, 2.2250738585072014e-308, 1.7976931348623157e308, -1.5, 3.0 (stays a number) |
   624	| boolean | true, false |
   625	| datetime | 0, a negative instant, 1700000000000.5 (fractional millisecond), the earliest and latest instant Triplex accepts |
   626	| ref | same type, another type, an entity created in the same command |
   627	| json | {"b":1,"a":2} (key order kept), nested arrays and objects, non-ASCII text, 1e300 |
   628	| blob | descriptor with and without filename, size 0, a size above 2^32 |
