   638	### 7.3 Fault points (CS-FAULT)
   639	
   640	The expected outcome after a fault is chosen from the last transition with durable or engine-side evidence observed by the fault injector after the crash (the log file's records read back, the engine's committed transactions, the publication marker), never from the system's own claim. A transition the protocol declares but the receipt does not witness fails the case.
   641	
   642	**qlever transitions.**
   643	
   644	| Transition | Witness evidence |
   645	| --- | --- |
   646	| QT0-RECEIVED | broker request log entry |
   647	| QT1-VALIDATED | group member accepted against staged state (broker trace) |
   648	| QT2-LOGGED | COMMIT record present in the log file after restart (fsync completed); this is the irrevocable decision |
   649	| QT3-APPLY-SENT | update operation sent (broker trace) |
   650	| QT4-PUBLISHED | publication marker for the group's P visible in a query |
   651	| QT5-VERIFIED | complete expected effects and absences checked (broker trace and independent query through three access paths) |
   652	| QT6-ACKED | caller received the success receipt |
   653	
   654	**qlever expected outcomes.**
   655	
   656	| Fault after | Final state | Original caller | Retry with the same commandId | Reads |
   657	| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
   658	| QT0-RECEIVED or QT1-VALIDATED (no QT2 evidence) | the command is absent unless a later attempt commits it; it is never committed twice | typed failure or E-OUTCOME-UNKNOWN; never success | evaluated as a fresh command (commits at most once in total) | - |
   659	| QT2-LOGGED (no QT4 evidence) | the group MUST be published by recovery with the position decided at QT2; it can never become absent | E-OUTCOME-UNKNOWN or E-COMMIT-PENDING; never success before publication | before publication: E-COMMIT-PENDING or E-REPAIRING; after publication: the original success receipt (same txId and position) | never show the group before publication; E-REPAIRING while fenced |
   660	| QT3-APPLY-SENT (no QT4 evidence) | as QT2-LOGGED; partial permutation state must not be served: the lane fences and recovery re-applies or rebuilds | as QT2-LOGGED | as QT2-LOGGED | E-REPAIRING while fenced; after recovery all access paths agree |
   661	| QT4-PUBLISHED (no QT5 evidence) | published; recovery completes verification before any new write | E-OUTCOME-UNKNOWN or success; success only if publication was established | the original success receipt once publication is established, else E-REPAIRING | may show the group; E-REPAIRING while fenced |
   662	| QT5-VERIFIED failure (verification mismatch) | lane fenced; recovery republishes the logged state; final state equals O-REPLAY with the group present | no success until recovery establishes publication | E-REPAIRING until recovered, then the original success receipt | E-REPAIRING while fenced |
   663	| QT5-VERIFIED (no QT6 evidence): lost ACK | published | E-OUTCOME-UNKNOWN | the original success receipt | show the group |
   664	
   665	A success receipt is valid only if its timestamp is after the group's QT4-PUBLISHED evidence; a read by the same client issued after the success receipt sees the group (read-your-writes).
   666	
   667	**xtdb transitions.**
   668	
   669	| Transition | Witness evidence |
   670	| --- | --- |
   671	| XT0-RECEIVED | client trace |
   672	| XT1-BEGIN-SENT | driver trace |
   673	| XT2-ENGINE-COMMITTED | the transaction is committed in the engine after restart (operation marker row present at its position) |
   674	| XT3-ACKED | caller received the success receipt |
   675	
   676	**xtdb expected outcomes.**
   677	
   678	| Fault after | Final state | Original caller | Retry with the same commandId | Reads |
   679	| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
   680	| XT0 or XT1 (no XT2 evidence) | absent unless a later attempt commits it; never committed twice | typed failure or E-OUTCOME-UNKNOWN; never success | evaluated as a fresh command | - |
   681	| XT2-ENGINE-COMMITTED (no XT3 evidence): lost ACK | present exactly once at its position | E-OUTCOME-UNKNOWN; resolution through EP-RESOLVE returns committed | E-COMMAND-COMMITTED carrying the original txId (or the original receipt) | show the transaction (publication is atomic with commit) |
   682	
   683	A success receipt is valid only after XT2 evidence; read-your-writes holds for the same client.
   684	
   685	Access paths verified after each fault: XTDB `_id` lookup and column-predicate scan; QLever subject, predicate-object and object scans; plus the repository, the native surface in every language of the engine and the raw recipe.
