   688	
   689	- Schema: at least three EntityTypes using all eight families, cardinality one and many, required, optional, unique, a ref with target type and a reverse ref; two releases (v2 adds an optional attribute and a constraint).
   690	- Command stream: create; correction; card-many add and remove; future validTo crossing later; retraction; with enforcement off, equal duplicates (one value, two supports) and distinct-value conflicts and overlapping intervals; presence toggles (convention until the Q9 policy); two commits sharing one recorded instant; a second runtime with a lagging clock; one nested transaction with two positions; the v2 release.
   691	- Cut catalog: every phase position, recorded instants between and at commits (including the decreasing one), valid instants at, before and after every boundary; frozen from the oracle's derived positions, checked against receipts.
   692	- Operations at each cut: get; getMany with missing ids; find with equality, range, membership and ref predicates per family, include, order, limit and cursor continuation; timeline; at(basis) for current, past R, past V and both. Conflicts expect E-CONFLICTING-VALUES per C5.
   693	- Modes: current, reopen, engine restart. Size: a hand-built core of at most 200 entities plus a seeded generated variant.
