   699	### 7.6 Cursor and basis continuation (CS-CURSOR)
   700	
   701	A cursor or a requested historical basis issued before any transition below continues successfully afterward (through the exact ledger path where the projection changed), returning exactly the rows O-REPLAY computes at the cursor's basis. An available retained cut never becomes unavailable because its projection, mapping or index changed. No retention policy exists, so 'cut no longer retained' is never a permitted outcome.
   702	
   703	| Must continue | Transition |
   704	| --- | --- |
   705	| CT-ENGINE-RESTART | engine restart |
   706	| CT-CLIENT-REOPEN | fresh runtime and client on the same scope |
   707	| CT-RELEASE-CHANGE | a new schema release is published; the cursor continues under its own release's mapping |
   708	| CT-PROJECTION-REBUILD | projection rebuilt or backfilled |
   709	| CT-GENERATION-SWITCH | projection or index generation switch |
   710	| CT-PUBLICATION-ADVANCE | newer commits published after the cursor's P |
   711	| CT-MAINTAINING | QLever marker in MAINTAINING |
   712	| CT-BOUNDARY-PASS | a valid-time boundary passes after the cursor was issued |
   713	| CT-COMPACTION | XTDB compaction or GC, QLever rebuild-index or checkpoint |
   714	| CT-BROKER-FAILOVER | broker replaced and recovery completed |
   715	| CT-BACKUP-RESTORE | restore into a fresh engine from a backup taken after the cursor was issued |
   716	| CT-FENCE-RECOVERED | lane fenced, then recovered: during the fence E-REPAIRING is permitted; after recovery the same cursor must continue |
   717	
   718	| Permitted error case | Error | Reason | Only when |
   719	| --- | --- | --- | --- |
   720	| CE-MALFORMED | E-CURSOR | malformed | the token was altered or is not a token |
   721	| CE-OTHER-SCOPE | E-CURSOR | other-scope | the cursor belongs to another scope |
   722	| CE-OTHER-QUERY | E-CURSOR | other-query | the cursor belongs to a query with a different definition hash |
   723	| CE-FUTURE-BASIS | E-UNAVAILABLE-CUT | unavailable-cut | the requested position is beyond the latest committed position |
   724	| CE-FENCED | E-REPAIRING | repairing | only while the lane is fenced; the case also asserts continuation after recovery |
