   745	### 8.2 Golden scenario rules (TARGETS section 6)
   746	
   747	- A seeded, deterministic generator produces the command stream and the reads; the same seed gives the same bytes.
   748	- Expected answers come from O-REPLAY or a frozen hand derivation (O-HAND), never from a system under test.
   749	- Unless a scenario says otherwise it runs on P-YEAR-ONE with the fixed writer trace running and 256 concurrent pinned readers (P-NS).
   750	- A scenario fails on any wrong answer, any lost or duplicated commit, any feed gap or order violation, or any missed bar; its receipt records the correctness verdicts and the P1 to P5 measurements together.
   751	- All 20 run on every composition being compared, and the final acceptance reruns all 20 fresh.
   752	- Numbers inside the scenarios: pay rates, hours and money use scaled integers or order-preserving decimal strings; the scenarios include the range rules 'pay rate at or above 16.50' and 'hours over 40' (cases GS-NUM-RANGE-1650 and GS-NUM-HOURS-40, selected by GS.18's dashboard filters) and at least one write of a value the lane cannot hold, which must fail with E-VALUE-OUT-OF-RANGE or E-DECIMAL-UNREPRESENTABLE (GS-NUM-UNHOLDABLE, selected by GS.02).
